From: Jean Iaquinta <jeani@uio.no>
Subject: [PATCH] MPIR_Datatype_get_elements_x(): guard divide-by-zero

Guard against (type1_sz + type2_sz) == 0 for struct datatypes with mixed
basic types before computing usable_bytes / (type1_sz + type2_sz).

Backported from pmodels/mpich PR https://github.com/pmodels/mpich/pull/7202
(merged upstream after 4.3.2 / 5.0.2rc2).
Upstream: https://github.com/pmodels/mpich/pull/7202

--- a/src/mpi/datatype/get_elements_x.c
+++ b/src/mpi/datatype/get_elements_x.c
@@ -97,6 +97,12 @@
     }
 
     /* determine the number of elements in the region */
+    if (type1_sz + type2_sz == 0) {
+        /* this is likely a struct type with mixed basic elements. Let's just bail for now */
+        *bytes_p = 0;
+        return 0;
+    }
+
     elements = 2 * (usable_bytes / (type1_sz + type2_sz));
     if (usable_bytes % (type1_sz + type2_sz) >= type1_sz)
         elements++;
